Round 1 and round 2 PCBs arrived simultaneously, so we decided to go straight to round 2 PCB. 

Soldering was done using solder paste via stencil and reflow oven. There was bridging on the micro USB port and buck converter, but this was solved using flux and a soldering iron. 
All connections were checked for continuity. 
Programming was done via the USB port, and was successful. 
Motor and solenoid drivers were tested and working. Servo output was tested and working. SPI devices were not tested, as we do not have them at the moment. 
